research/audit/wave8-judge-adjudications.jsonl:1:{"id":"thm-infinite-product-criterion","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"758abfc228969b2ea954c97072d36b8a4bcdb9246edc7093b23db9dd11cdde43","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"f06362e6e85a0cdd12ea0ddd951f8eba54914d0c9f43dac3e96d0a669a34f27e","verdict_item_sha256":"76262862432c1d9757e46e87a23864cf2b5771e7ccf54cbf56d6970825b5e583","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"Terra correctly identifies a local citation omission: lem-of-abs-value states verbatim '$|x| \\ge 0; \\quad |x| = 0 \\iff x = 0; \\quad -|x| \\le x \\le |x|; \\quad |-x| = |x|; \\quad |xy| = |x|\\,|y|$' and does not state the triangle inequality. But lem-of-triangle-inequality states verbatim '$|x + y| \\le |x| + |y|$'; substituting that standard inequality in steps 1.4 and 4.3 closes the citation gap immediately and changes no inference. This is a minor citation quirk below the binding thirty-second threshold, so R1 licenses no edit."}
research/audit/wave8-judge-adjudications.jsonl:2:{"id":"cex-cauchy-product-of-convergent-series-diverges","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"c4a69a501d90076bd7fbba2ceee697175c09e82e847160708cf5f9ea94b76e48","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","item_sha256":"11d563ad2d6ea1161518a184cd7f4d7c0441fe5c8a04e1db5b429ce9bd6bc9ad","verdict_item_sha256":"0e601b43ae73646f5a3aca81ff9621c05f94d8e0212252f764661253885a3eaf","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"Terra correctly spots an omitted Archimedean bridge in the explanatory step 2.2. The exact library result cor-archimedean-reciprocal says verbatim, 'For every epsilon > 0 in a complete ordered field there is a natural n >= 1 with 1/n < epsilon.' Given r < 2, apply it to the positive bound (2-r)/2 and then use [L3] to pass to later canonical naturals; this gives 2-2/iota(n+2) > r. The repair is a seconds-long standard lookup, the displayed lower bound and divergence proof are unchanged, and R1 licenses no edit."}
