research/audit/wave8-judge-adjudications.jsonl:7:{"id":"cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"6c8c857e5d4fe3bf46e1842f8ff940ad591b548ccef8a5459ae69f598c177a5f","outcome":"confirmed_fatal","defect_type":"other","item_sha256":"0c233b550b97c24e0a2260aee6c6a5567188595839a2ca772764d23f3c2b61f5","verdict_item_sha256":"8dfaf08dc3d49e97498b13ecc81fda7bcf6c3037967d65b8e058c906aa066629","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh; owner-delegated)","at":"2026-08-09T08:03:46Z","note":"Confirmed as a false reader-visible Facts assertion, not a proof-step gap. L1 says verbatim, 'an at most countable family may be presented as a sequence indexed by N'; for the empty family no function N -> emptyset exists. def-countable only says, 'A is at most countable if it is finite or countably infinite,' and its own Remark directs the nonempty enumeration equivalence to lem-countable-iff-surjection-from-n. The binding thirty-second rule applies to logical gaps, not false general assertions. The clause is unused: step 1.2 instead invokes the preceding exact fact Q approximately N to choose beta:N -> Q. The minimal licensed repair is therefore to delete only the false clause and its now-unused direct dependency/citation, leaving every theorem claim and proof step unchanged."}
