research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/cor-no-function-is-continuous-exactly-on-q.md-722-kind: theorem
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/cor-no-function-is-continuous-exactly-on-q.md:723:title: "The Dirichlet function is continuous at no point of $\\mathbb{R}$, and Thomae's function is continuous at every irrational and at no rational, so its set of continuity points is exactly the set of irrationals and its oscillation at $c$ equals $t(c)$"
