research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/cor-no-function-is-continuous-exactly-on-q.md:791:[L5] $\omega_{f}(S) = \sup\{|f(x)-f(y)| : x,y \in S\}$ and $\omega_{f}(c) = \inf\{\omega_{f}(N_\delta(c)) : \delta > 0\}$ for $f$ defined on all of $\mathbb{R}$, both computed in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$, where every set has a supremum and an infimum; $f$ is continuous at $c$ if and only if $\omega_{f}(c) = 0$ ([[def-oscillation]], [[def-extended-reals]], [[lem-extended-reals-complete]], [[thm-continuity-iff-oscillation-zero]]).
