research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-8-{"id":"thm-continuous-inverse","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.csudh.edu/~pong/a3/Notes_10.html"],"rationale":"The university notes state exactly that a strictly monotone function on an interval has a continuous inverse on its image and pair it with the continuous-injection theorem used here.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-9-{"id":"cor-cantor-function-is-continuous","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor_function"],"rationale":"The source states exactly that the Cantor function is continuous on the unit interval.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-10-{"id":"rem-cantor-function-increases-only-on-a-null-set","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor_function"],"rationale":"The source records that the Cantor function is constant off the null Cantor set while increasing from zero to one. The item reformulates “increase only” without importing derivative or absolute-continuity machinery.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:11:{"id":"def-oscillation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscillation_(mathematics)"],"rationale":"The source gives oscillation on a set and at a point by local suprema/infima. The item uses the equivalent pairwise-difference supremum, extended-real empty-set conventions, relative domains, and bounded-function clauses.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:12:{"id":"thm-continuity-iff-oscillation-zero","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Real_Function_is_Continuous_at_Point_iff_Oscillation_is_Zero"],"rationale":"The source states exactly, for f:D→R and x∈D, that continuity at x is equivalent to zero oscillation with the same neighbourhood-relative definition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:13:{"id":"lem-oscillation-superlevel-sets-are-closed","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscillation_(mathematics)"],"rationale":"The source explains that oscillation superlevel sets are closed and continuity points form a G-delta. The item supplies the relative-domain trace formulation and a fully local closure proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:14:{"id":"thm-discontinuity-set-is-f-sigma","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classification_of_discontinuities","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%CE%B4_set"],"rationale":"The sources state that every real function has an F-sigma discontinuity set and G-delta continuity set. The item spells out the oscillation thresholds and relative-domain trace form.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-15-{"id":"def-dirichlet-and-thomae-functions","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomae%27s_function","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_function"],"rationale":"The sources give exactly the Dirichlet indicator and Thomae denominator functions, including the reduced positive-denominator convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-16-{"id":"thm-dirichlet-and-thomae-continuity-sets","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomae%27s_function","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_function"],"rationale":"The sources state exactly that the Dirichlet function is nowhere continuous and Thomae’s function is continuous precisely at irrational points.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-17-{"id":"thm-continuity-set-realisation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%CE%B4_set","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classification_of_discontinuities"],"rationale":"The standard characterization says that the continuity sets of real functions are exactly the G-delta subsets of R. The item realizes the set through decreasing open sets and opposite rational/irrational signs, with explicit empty/full boundary cases.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
