research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6026-          ]
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6027-        },
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6028-        {
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:6029:          "id": "ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed-step-1-2",
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6030-          "claim": "Claim 2: let $q \\ge 1$ be a natural and put $x := 1/\\iota(q)$. Then $\\iota(q)x = 1 \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, so $q \\in Q(x)$ and $q(x) \\le q$. Conversely, if $1 \\le k \\le q$ is a natural with $\\iota(k)x = \\iota(k)/\\iota(q) \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, then $k < q$ would put $\\iota(k)/\\iota(q)$ strictly between $0$ and $1$, which no integer is; so $k = q$. Hence $q(x) = q$ and $t(1/\\iota(q)) = 1/\\iota(q)$. Taking $q = 2$ gives $t(1/2) = 1/2$. [A1, L2]",
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6031-          "step": "1.2",
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6032-          "inputs": [
--
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6035-          ]
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6036-        },
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6037-        {
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:6038:          "id": "ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed-step-1-3",
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6039-          "claim": "Claim 3: put $x := 2/3$. Then $\\iota(3)x = 2 \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, so $q(x) \\le 3$. Also $\\iota(1)x = 2/3$ lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and so is not an integer, and $\\iota(2)x = 4/3$ lies strictly between $1$ and $2$ and so is not an integer. Hence $q(x) = 3$ and $t(2/3) = 1/3$. [A1, L2]",
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6040-          "step": "1.3",
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-6041-          "inputs": [
