research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.result.json:16:  "tail": "ITEM: thm-baire-one-continuity-points\nVERDICT: CERTIFIED\nCURRENT-TEXT: READ\nMATHEMATICS: The direct refinement proof is valid: Baire yields a subinterval with uniformly small approximation error, and monotonicity transfers small set oscillation to its interior points, contradicting any interval contained in \\(D_\\varepsilon\\).\nCITATIONS: Internal dependencies license the closed-superlevel, \\(F_\\sigma/G_\\delta\\), and interval-category steps. Both external references support the stated Baire-one/category result: [Baire function](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_function), [Baire category theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_category_theorem).\nMETADATA: Normalized hash matches dispatch: `5db1f9a5e25ddbee920e0a5415834fd29db78a26111147dc95392d4aa2a43378`. Provenance is ai-altered/ai-altered; the removed continuity–oscillation dependency is absent, and no stale judge/audited/verified block remains.\nFINDINGS: NONE"
