research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-226-      "claim": "Claim 3: put $x := 2/3$. Then $\\iota(3)x = 2 \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, so $q(x) \\le 3$. Also $\\iota(1)x = 2/3$ lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and so is not an integer, and $\\iota(2)x = 4/3$ lies strictly between $1$ and $2$ and so is not an integer. Hence $q(x) = 3$ and $t(2/3) = 1/3$. [A1, L2]",
