research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-244-      "claim": "Claim 5: $\\omega_{t}(c) = t(c)$ at every real $c$. At an integer $m$ this is $1$ by step 1.1; at a real of the form $m + 1/2$ with $m$ an integer, the least denominator is $2$, by the same computation as in step 1.2 applied to $\\iota(2)(m + 1/2) = 2m + 1 \\in \\mathbb{Z}$ together with $\\iota(1)(m + 1/2) = m + 1/2$ lying strictly between $m$ and $m+1$, so the value is $1/2$; and at an irrational it is $0$. [step 1.1, step 1.2, step 1.4, A1, L1, L2]",
