research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1182-[L1] $f$ is continuous at $c$ exactly when for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a real $\delta > 0$ with $|f(x) - f(c)| < \varepsilon$ for every $x \in A$ with $|x - c| < \delta$; equivalently for every $x \in A \cap N_\delta(c)$ ([[def-continuity-real]], [[def-neighbourhood-r]]).
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1183-
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md:1184:[L2] $\omega_f(S) = \sup\{|f(x) - f(y)| : x, y \in S\}$ and $\omega_f(c) = \inf\{\omega_f(A \cap N_\delta(c)) : \delta > 0\}$, both in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$; $0 \le \omega_f(c) \le \omega_f(A \cap N_\delta(c))$ for every real $\delta > 0$, and $c \in A \cap N_\delta(c)$ ([[def-oscillation]], [[def-extended-reals]]).
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1185-
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1186-[L3] In $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ every subset has a least upper bound and a greatest lower bound; a supremum is at most an extended real $u$ exactly when $u$ bounds every member of the set, and an infimum is at least an extended real $\ell$ exactly when $\ell$ bounds every member from below ([[lem-extended-reals-complete]]).
