research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md:1215:- **The oscillation measures how badly continuity fails, not merely whether it
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1216-  does.** The theorem uses only whether $\omega_f(c)$ vanishes, but the number
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md:1217:  itself carries more: the oscillation of Thomae's function at a point $c$ is
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1218-  proved below to be exactly $t(c)$
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1219-  ([[thm-dirichlet-and-thomae-continuity-sets]]), so it is $1/q$ at a rational
research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed.md-1220-  with least denominator $q$ and $0$ at every irrational.
