research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/thm-froda.md:1577:title: "The Dirichlet function is continuous at no point of $\\mathbb{R}$, and Thomae's function is continuous at every irrational and at no rational, so its set of continuity points is exactly the set of irrationals and its oscillation at $c$ equals $t(c)$"
