research/audit/wave9-refuter-tasks/thm-continuity-iff-oscillation-zero.md-1239-[L2] In $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ every subset has a greatest lower bound; an infimum is $\ge$ an extended real $\ell$ exactly when $\ell$ bounds the set from below, and the infimum is $\le$ every member of the set ([[lem-extended-reals-complete]]).
