research/audit/wave9-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-lem-oscillation-superlevel-sets-are-closed.prompt.md:129:[L1] $\omega_f(S) = \sup\{|f(x) - f(y)| : x, y \in S\}$ in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$, and $\omega_f(S) \le \omega_f(T)$ whenever $S \subseteq T \subseteq A$; for $c \in A$, $\omega_f(c) = \inf\{\omega_f(A \cap N_\delta(c)) : \delta > 0\}$ ([[def-oscillation]], [[def-extended-reals]]).
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-lem-oscillation-superlevel-sets-are-closed.prompt.md-130-
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-lem-oscillation-superlevel-sets-are-closed.prompt.md-131-[L2] In $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ every subset has a greatest lower bound; an infimum is $\ge$ an extended real $\ell$ exactly when $\ell$ bounds the set from below, and the infimum is $\le$ every member of the set ([[lem-extended-reals-complete]]).
