research/audit/wave9-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-ex-locally-unbounded-finite-everywhere.prompt.md-1991-- **The continuity set of $t$ is $G_\delta$, as it must be.** The irrationals form a $G_\delta$ set ([[cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta]]), in agreement with [[thm-discontinuity-set-is-f-sigma]]. The reverse arrangement is impossible: no function is continuous at every rational and discontinuous at every irrational, because $\mathbb{Q}$ is not $G_\delta$ ([[cor-no-function-is-continuous-exactly-on-q]]).
