research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-3946-[L1] $f$ of Baire class one on $[a,b]$ means: there are continuous $f_k : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}$ with $f_k(x) \to f(x)$ for every $x \in [a,b]$ ([[def-baire-class-one]], [[def-continuity-real]], [[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]]).
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-3947-
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log:3948:[L2] $\omega_f(S) = \sup\{|f(x)-f(y)| : x,y \in S\}$; $\omega_f(x) = \inf\{\omega_f([a,b] \cap N_\delta(x)) : \delta > 0\}$; $\omega_f$ is monotone under inclusion and $\omega_f(x) \ge 0$ ([[def-oscillation]]).
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-3949-
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log:3950:[L4] For every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a closed $G \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ with $\{x \in [a,b] : \omega_f(x) \ge \varepsilon\} = [a,b] \cap G$ ([[lem-oscillation-superlevel-sets-are-closed]]).
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-3951-
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-3952-[L5] If $a < b$, $(F_n)$ are closed and $[a,b] \subseteq \bigcup_n F_n$, then some $F_n \cap [a,b]$ contains a nondegenerate closed interval ([[lem-baire-category-in-a-closed-interval]]).
