research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log:4679:  itself carries more: the oscillation of Thomae's function at a point $c$ is
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-4680-  proved below to be exactly $t(c)$
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-4681-  ([[thm-dirichlet-and-thomae-continuity-sets]]), so it is $1/q$ at a rational
research/audit/wave9-dispatch/certifier-a6r2-thm-baire-one-continuity-points.log-4682-  with least denominator $q$ and $0$ at every irrational.
