research/audit/wave9-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-thm-discontinuity-set-is-f-sigma.prompt.md-1854-[L1] $f$ of Baire class one on $[a,b]$ means: there are continuous $f_k : [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}$ with $f_k(x) \to f(x)$ for every $x \in [a,b]$ ([[def-baire-class-one]], [[def-continuity-real]], [[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]]).
