research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-5-{"id":"thm-froda","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discontinuities_of_monotone_functions"],"rationale":"The source states exactly that the discontinuity set of a monotone real function on an interval is at most countable and gives the same rational-in-each-jump injection.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-6-{"id":"thm-monotone-with-prescribed-discontinuity-set","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discontinuities_of_monotone_functions"],"rationale":"The jump-functions section constructs a nondecreasing sum of summable step functions with discontinuities at a prescribed countable set. The item extends the presentation to every at-most-countable subset of R and fixes explicit weights and empty/finite cases.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-7-{"id":"thm-continuous-injection-on-an-interval-is-strictly-monotone","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Continuous_Injection_of_Interval_is_Strictly_Monotone"],"rationale":"The source states exactly that a continuous injective real function on an interval is strictly monotone.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-8-{"id":"thm-continuous-inverse","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.csudh.edu/~pong/a3/Notes_10.html"],"rationale":"The university notes state exactly that a strictly monotone function on an interval has a continuous inverse on its image and pair it with the continuous-injection theorem used here.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-9-{"id":"cor-cantor-function-is-continuous","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor_function"],"rationale":"The source states exactly that the Cantor function is continuous on the unit interval.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-10-{"id":"rem-cantor-function-increases-only-on-a-null-set","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor_function"],"rationale":"The source records that the Cantor function is constant off the null Cantor set while increasing from zero to one. The item reformulates “increase only” without importing derivative or absolute-continuity machinery.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:11:{"id":"def-oscillation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscillation_(mathematics)"],"rationale":"The source gives oscillation on a set and at a point by local suprema/infima. The item uses the equivalent pairwise-difference supremum, extended-real empty-set conventions, relative domains, and bounded-function clauses.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:12:{"id":"thm-continuity-iff-oscillation-zero","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Real_Function_is_Continuous_at_Point_iff_Oscillation_is_Zero"],"rationale":"The source states exactly, for f:D→R and x∈D, that continuity at x is equivalent to zero oscillation with the same neighbourhood-relative definition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:13:{"id":"lem-oscillation-superlevel-sets-are-closed","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscillation_(mathematics)"],"rationale":"The source explains that oscillation superlevel sets are closed and continuity points form a G-delta. The item supplies the relative-domain trace formulation and a fully local closure proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:14:{"id":"thm-discontinuity-set-is-f-sigma","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classification_of_discontinuities","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%CE%B4_set"],"rationale":"The sources state that every real function has an F-sigma discontinuity set and G-delta continuity set. The item spells out the oscillation thresholds and relative-domain trace form.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-15-{"id":"def-dirichlet-and-thomae-functions","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomae%27s_function","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_function"],"rationale":"The sources give exactly the Dirichlet indicator and Thomae denominator functions, including the reduced positive-denominator convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-16-{"id":"thm-dirichlet-and-thomae-continuity-sets","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomae%27s_function","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_function"],"rationale":"The sources state exactly that the Dirichlet function is nowhere continuous and Thomae’s function is continuous precisely at irrational points.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-17-{"id":"thm-continuity-set-realisation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%CE%B4_set","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classification_of_discontinuities"],"rationale":"The standard characterization says that the continuity sets of real functions are exactly the G-delta subsets of R. The item realizes the set through decreasing open sets and opposite rational/irrational signs, with explicit empty/full boundary cases.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-18-{"id":"cor-no-function-is-continuous-exactly-on-q","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%CE%B4_set","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_category_theorem"],"rationale":"The sources establish that continuity sets are G-delta and that Q is not G-delta by Baire category. The item is the direct library corollary with the canonical-copy convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-19-{"id":"def-intermediate-value-property","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Darboux_property"],"rationale":"The Encyclopedia of Mathematics gives the classical pointwise Darboux property. The item merges that form with the equivalent arbitrary-interval/every-subinterval image formulation, so it is a semantic adaptation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-20-{"id":"def-semicontinuity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semi-continuity"],"rationale":"The source gives upper and lower semicontinuity and their limsup/liminf forms. The item fixes strict epsilon inequalities on arbitrary real subdomains and adds equivalent neighbourhood envelopes.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-21-{"id":"thm-semicontinuity-level-set-characterisation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semi-continuity","https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Characterization_of_Lower_Semicontinuity"],"rationale":"The sources give the closed/open level-set characterizations of semicontinuity. The item packages strict and non-strict relative level sets and the continuity-as-both consequence.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-22-{"id":"thm-semicontinuous-evt","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Real-Valued_Upper_Semicontinuous_Function_on_Compact_Space_attains_Maximum_with_Compact_Set_of_Maximizers","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semi-continuity"],"rationale":"The source states exactly that an upper semicontinuous real function on a nonempty compact space attains its maximum, with the lower/minimum statement obtained dually.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-23-{"id":"lem-baire-category-in-a-closed-interval","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_category_theorem"],"rationale":"Baire category says a nonempty complete interval cannot be covered by countably many closed sets with empty relative interior. The item writes the equivalent nondegenerate-subinterval conclusion in real-line notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-24-{"id":"def-baire-class-one","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Baire_classes","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_function"],"rationale":"The sources define Baire class one as pointwise limits of sequences of continuous functions; the Wikipedia convention, followed by the item, includes continuous functions themselves.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:25:{"id":"thm-baire-one-continuity-points","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_function","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_category_theorem"],"rationale":"The sources state that a Baire-one function has a dense G-delta continuity set and meager discontinuity set. The item strengthens the presentation with closed oscillation superlevels containing no interval and a relative [a,b] formulation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-26-{"id":"def-additive-function","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cauchy%27s_functional_equation"],"rationale":"The source gives exactly Cauchy’s equation f(x+y)=f(x)+f(y) and names its solutions additive functions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-27-{"id":"lem-additive-is-q-linear","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cauchy%27s_functional_equation"],"rationale":"The source states exactly that every additive map satisfies f(qx)=qf(x) for rational q.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-28-{"id":"lem-additive-bounded-above-on-an-interval-is-linear","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00010-025-01210-4"],"rationale":"The peer-reviewed source states exactly that an additive real function bounded above on a nondegenerate open interval is linear.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-29-{"id":"thm-cauchy-functional-equation-regularity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cauchy%27s_functional_equation","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00010-025-01210-4"],"rationale":"The sources list the standard regularity conditions forcing additive functions to be linear and the dense-graph alternative. The item combines six equivalent conditions, both signs, and the explicit dense-graph conclusion in one theorem.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-30-{"id":"lem-hamel-basis-exists","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HamelBasis.html"],"rationale":"The source gives existence of a Hamel basis of R over Q under choice and unique finite rational coordinates. The item additionally develops coefficient maps, kernels, fibres, and their algebraic properties.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-31-{"id":"fs-intermediate-value-property-implies-continuity","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Darboux_property"],"rationale":"The source explicitly records that the intermediate value property does not imply continuity and gives the standard sin(1/x) witness. The item adapts that construction to the library's nearest-integer-distance oscillator psi(1/x), so the local refutation is source-adapted rather than verbatim.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-32-{"id":"fs-additive-implies-linear","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cauchy%27s_functional_equation","https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HamelBasis.html"],"rationale":"The sources state exactly that, assuming choice, Hamel bases produce additive functions not of the form cx.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:33:{"id":"ex-thomae-values-and-oscillation-computed","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomae%27s_function","https://mathworld.wolfram.com/DirichletFunction.html"],"rationale":"The sources give Thomae’s values and continuity behaviour; the exact oscillation computation 1/q and the bounded-range clauses are a locally expanded semantic version.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-34-{"id":"ex-monotone-function-discontinuous-exactly-at-the-rationals","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.unm.edu/~crisp/courses/math402/spring19/hwk.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discontinuities_of_monotone_functions"],"rationale":"The university exercise gives the same weighted sum of rational step functions, monotone and discontinuous exactly at the rationals.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-35-{"id":"ex-froda-is-sharp","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discontinuities_of_monotone_functions"],"rationale":"The literature states the prescribed-countable-discontinuity construction, which immediately makes the at-most-countable Froda bound sharp. The item packages that consequence as a separate example.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-36-{"id":"ex-continuous-inverse-gives-the-nth-root","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~bishop/classes/math320.F21/lecOct21.pdf","https://math.csudh.edu/~pong/a3/Notes_10.html"],"rationale":"The notes treat nth roots through the continuous strictly increasing power map and its inverse. The item records the library’s precise nonnegative domain, endpoints, and inverse identity.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-37-{"id":"ex-cantor-function-maps-a-null-set-onto-the-unit-interval","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://researchers.ms.unimelb.edu.au/~xgge%40unimelb/Files/Teaching/Advanced%20Probability%20%28Semester%201%202020%29/The%20Cantor%20Function%20and%20the%20Cantor%20Set.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor_function"],"rationale":"The university notes state that the Cantor set is null and that the Cantor function maps it onto [0,1], exactly the example’s core claim.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-38-{"id":"ex-locally-unbounded-finite-everywhere","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.camden.rutgers.edu/files/Real_Analysis.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomae%27s_function"],"rationale":"The open real-analysis text gives the reduced-denominator Thomae construction. The item takes its reciprocal-denominator companion on the rationals, with a finite value on irrationals, and supplies the everywhere-local-unboundedness and denominator-separation proofs.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl-39-{"id":"ex-indicator-of-q-is-baire-class-two-not-one","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_function","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_function"],"rationale":"The sources state exactly that the Dirichlet indicator is Baire class two and not Baire class one because it is nowhere continuous.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
