research/audit/wave9-real-analysis.findings.md:85:> Thus `omega_f(S) <= 2M` for every `S subseteq A`. If `S` is nonempty, `omega_f(S)` is a real number in `[0,2M]`, and every point oscillation is also a real number in `[0,2M]`. The convention `omega_f(emptyset) = -infinity` remains the single empty-set exception. Apart from that exception, an infinite extended value can occur only when `f` is unbounded.
